When you save an image as a PNG file, the file size may be larger than other image formats, but the image quality will remain high. This makes PNG a popular choice for images that require a high level of detail, such as graphics, logos, and screenshots.

It's worth noting that the resolution of an image is determined by the number of pixels it contains, and PNG files can contain a large number of pixels, which allows them to retain high resolution."}

